{
  "text": "For Co-Primary Endpoint 1, 6-Month Closure Success, exact binomial testing at the one-sided 5% significance level will be performed against the performance goal (null hypothesis proportion).",
  "page": "",
  "section": "4.3.1 Test Method"
}

{
  "text": "Depending on the outcome of this test, Co-Primary Endpoint 2, Composite Clinical Success, will be tested by the same method.",
  "page": "",
  "section": "4.3.1 Test Method"
}

{
  "text": "In addition, the 95% one-sided Clopper-Pearson confidence interval lower bound will be reported.",
  "page": "",
  "section": "4.3.1 Test Method"
}

{
  "text": "The overall Type I error rate of 5% will be controlled for multiplicity by the following hierarchical testing structure",
  "page": "",
  "section": "4.3.2 Test Hierarchy for Multiplicity Control"
}

{
  "text": "An assessment of the poolability of the sites using a 2-by-(number of sites) contingency table of the primary outcome versus site. Fisher's Exact Test will be used to assess homogeneity.",
  "page": "",
