{
  "text": "PFS is defined as the time from date of randomization to the date of first documented disease progression as assessed by the IRC using Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors [RECIST] v1.1, or date of death due to any cause, whichever occurred first. Disease progression was defined as greater than or equal to (\u2265)20 percent (%) increase in sum of the diameter of target lesions, taking as reference the smallest sum diameter recorded since the treatment started.",
  "page": "",
  "section": "PRIMARY ANALYSIS"
}

{
  "text": "The primary efficacy analysis will be based on PFS as assessed by the IRC. The primary analysis will be performed using a stratified log-rank test stratified by the number of prior systemic therapies for advanced disease (1 vs \u22652) and presence of liver metastases (yes vs no) at a one-sided significance level of 0.025.",
  "page": "",
  "section": "PRIMARY ANALYSIS"
}

{
  "text": "The distribution of PFS will be estimated using the Kaplan-Meier method. Kaplan-Meier curves will be presented by treatment group and by subgroups defined by stratification factors. Median PFS and corresponding 95% confidence intervals will be provided for each treatment group.",
  "page": "",
  "section": "PRIMARY ANALYSIS"
}

{
  "text": "The hazard ratio and corresponding 95% confidence interval will be estimated using a stratified Cox proportional hazards model stratified by the number of prior systemic therapies for advanced disease (1 vs \u22652) and presence of liver metastases (yes vs no).",
