{
  "text": "The primary endpoints, Cmax and AUC0-t in fasting or fed group, will be log-transformed and a mixed-effects model will be applied. The model will include fixed effects for sequence, treatment, and period and a random effect of subject nested within sequence. Treatment differences on the log scale will be estimated for the parameters together with their 90% CIs. The least squares means together with their 95% CIs by treatment will also be estimated. Point estimates and CIs will be back-transformed to the original scale for presentation, i.e., ratios of geometric means and corresponding 90% CIs for Treatment A/Treatment B, geometric means and corresponding 95% CIs by treatment, respectively.",
