{
  "text": "Terminal elimination rate constant. Determined from the terminal slope of the log-transformed concentration curve using linear regression on terminal data points of the curve. The regression analysis should contain data from at least 3 different time points in the terminal phase consistent with the assessment of a straight line on the log-transformed scale. Phoenix WinNonlin best fit methodology will be used as standard. The Rsq should be \u22650.800 and the observation period over which the regression line is estimated should be at least two-fold the resulting t1/2 itself.",
